## 2026-07-03 - Phase 10.17a Scheduler Workflow Option Source Hotfix

- Patched `00042__skyserver_workflow_schedule_bridge_seed.sql` to seed the `skyserver_workflows` option source before assigning it to the Scheduler bridge tool parameter.
- Fixes existing-DB patch runs where `core.tool_parameters.option_source_code = skyserver_workflows` violated the `core.option_sources` foreign key.
- Keeps full `db_build` and incremental patch workflows aligned.


## Phase 10.17 — Workflow Lifecycle Simplification

- Simplified the user-facing workflow lifecycle to **ACTIVE / INACTIVE** instead of draft/archive/version-heavy controls.
- Added hard delete support for workflow definitions from Manage Workflows while preserving historical workflow run records where possible.
- Updated Workflows -> Start Workflow to use an active-workflow dropdown and remove runtime input JSON entry.
- Updated Manage Workflows so graph edits save the current sequential TOOL-node graph instead of exposing vNext/version publishing controls.
- Updated Scheduler bridge tool metadata so Start SkyServer Workflow can present active SkyServer workflows through a select-backed parameter option source.
- Added migration `00045__workflow_lifecycle_simplification.sql` for existing databases.
## Phase 10.16a — StatCan Concurrency / Retry Hotfix

- Tuned the upgraded StatCan ingestion primitive to use a safer default concurrency of 2 and source-specific max concurrency of 3.
- Added retry/backoff handling for retryable StatCan WDS HTTP failures, including HTTP 430 responses observed during higher-concurrency workflow runs.
- Updated the StatCan ingestion tool manifest prompt/defaults so workflow node parameter forms steer users toward the safer concurrency range.
- Added StatCan ingestion tuning variables to `.env.example`.

## Phase 10.10b — SkyWeb Alert Worker Seed Idempotency Hotfix

- Made `00030__skyweb_alert_worker_seed.sql` self-contained by seeding the Admin-owned `SKYWEB_ALERT_EVALUATE` permission before the `skyweb_alerts_evaluate` tool references it.
- Granted `SKYWEB_ALERT_EVALUATE` to Admin, Operator, and Super Admin roles when the SkyWeb alert worker seed is run manually against an existing database.
- Fixed full db_build seed ordering so `00030` no longer depends on the later `00041` permission hotfix seed.

## Phase 10.10a — Workflow Executor Permission Hotfix

- Added first-class SkyServer workflow permissions: `WORKFLOW_READ`, `WORKFLOW_START`, and `WORKFLOW_CANCEL`.
- Updated workflow API route guards to prefer SkyServer workflow permissions while retaining Temporal/Scheduler permissions as compatibility fallbacks.
- Updated the seeded `macro-refresh-pipeline` workflow definition to use `WORKFLOW_START` / `WORKFLOW_CANCEL` instead of Temporal-specific permissions.
- Added `SKYWEB_ALERT_EVALUATE` as the Admin-owned operational permission for the SkyWeb alert evaluation worker tool, avoiding cross-application permission-scope leakage from the public SkyWeb app.
- Updated Admin-Web Workflow Start permission checks and API error display so missing permission details are easier to diagnose.
- Added seed `00041__workflow_executor_permission_hotfix.sql` for existing databases.

## Phase 10.10 — SkyServer Workflow Executor v1

- Added `/api/workflows` endpoints for SkyServer workflow definitions, workflow starts, run history, and run detail.
- Added `workflowExecutorService`, which executes published SkyServer workflow definitions sequentially by node `display_order`.
- Added executor adapters for `TOOL` nodes and `TEMPORAL_WORKFLOW` nodes.
- Kept existing tools as first-class primitives by executing `TOOL` nodes through the same permission-aware script execution service used by Admin-Web Tools.
- Added Admin-Web Start Workflow and Workflow History pages for SkyServer workflow definitions and node-level run timelines.
- Preserved raw Temporal pages under `/workflows/temporal/start` and `/workflows/temporal/history` for lower-level runtime diagnostics.
- Added seed `00040__workflow_executor_v1_seed.sql` to mark the `macro-refresh-pipeline` foundation workflow as executor-v1 runnable and default its FRED node concurrency to 10.

## Phase 10.8 — Workflow Navigation Split

- Moved Temporal workflow navigation out of Automation and into a new top-level Workflows menu.
- Split the Temporal Admin-Web surface into `/workflows/start` for approved starts and `/workflows/history` for run inspection/history.
- Redirected legacy `/automation/temporal` and `/temporal` links to Workflow History.
- Renamed Tools -> Execution History to Tools History.
- Moved Audit under Access Control as User History and added `/access-control/user-history` with legacy audit redirects.
- Reordered the authenticated top menu to Dashboard, Tools, Workflows, Automation, Data, Configuration, Access Control.
- Added navbar/dropdown grouping styles for a cleaner control-plane menu.

## Phase 10.2 — Temporal FRED Indicator Workflow

- Converted `fredIngestionWorkflow` from one giant FRED script activity into per-indicator Temporal activity orchestration.
- Added `listFredIndicatorsActivity` for active FRED indicator discovery and `loadFredIndicatorActivity` for one-indicator download/normalize/load execution.
- Added controlled workflow concurrency with a default of 3 and a hard cap of 10.
